<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1100" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγών-ιος</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
				the contest</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄεθλος ἀ.</span>
			<i>its</i> prize, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				5(4).7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>O.</u>
					10(11).6
				</span></i>
			&lt;*&gt;; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					29
				</span></i>
			:— epith. of Hermes as <i>president of games</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				1.60
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(1).658
			</span></i>; of Zeus as <i>decider of the contest</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				26
			</span></i>:—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. θεοί</span>, in
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				513
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				189
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				242
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				783a
			</span></i>, either gods <i>in assembly</i>, or the gods <i>who
				presided over the great games</i> (Zeus, Poseidon, Apollo, and
			Hermes), 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγοραῖοι θ.</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1335.58
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγωνίῳ σχολᾷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj</u>
					104
				</span></i>
			, either <i>pause from battle</i>, or <i>strenuous
			rest</i> (oxymoron, cf. Sch.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
